 *   **Output:** A final image composed of fragments with color and opacity.
 
 **Data Structures:**
-*   **Tetrahedron Stream:** Each tetrahedron is sent to the GPU as a single point primitive. The vertex position is the position of one vertex (e.g., $v_0$). The other three vertices ($v_1, v_2, v_3$) are passed as texture coordinates. The scalar value of the primary vertex is passed as the $w$ coordinate of the vertex attribute [S2, unofficial].
-*   **Sorting Buffer:** An array of indices representing the sorted order of tetrahedra. This can be stored in a Vertex Buffer Object (VBO) on the GPU or streamed from CPU memory if it exceeds VRAM [S2, unofficial].
